caravan[0] | 6, 6, 16, 16 | The head of a caravan, drawn in front of its pack animals. Row 0 is a walking frame, the first and fifth of the caravan's eight-step cycle, and the only one drawn once the caravan reaches its destination. Used when travelling north. Turned a quarter, half and three quarters clockwise, it serves east, south and west.
